Fillets: the plate of a corner with a rider is oriented from a stripe
that rides on no line (mitcad#1532).

The roof slab rounded on all its edges with 0.66 to 0.86: at the left
eave's obtuse edge's ends the obtuse edge's rounding rides on the tip's
contact line (0016), the underside's end edge on the slope's line, and the
eave's end edge meets both. PerformMoreThreeCorner (1640, G0 constraints)
took the orientation of the plate's curves from the corner's first stripe,
here the obtuse edge's rider: its side on the line has its transition from
the line's support (RideOnOverlap, 1640), and the plate's face came out
with its wire the wrong way round (area -0.34 at r = 0.8). At the right
eave the tip is the rider and the corner's first stripe is not.

- PerformMoreThreeCorner: the orientation of the plate's p-curves (orien)
  is taken from the first stripe at the corner that rides on no other's
  line (the first one where all ride).

